  {
    "id": "reel-ex12-slip-cordon",
    "type": "reel",
    "when": "2026-11-20T19:30:00+05:30",
    "media": [
      "media/reel-ex12-slip-cordon/1-reel.mp4"
    ],
    "cover": "media/reel-ex12-slip-cordon/2-cover.jpg",
    "caption": "Three slips. And it still goes through the gap. 🏏\n\nA thin edge flies fine to the keeper and first slip. A thicker one flies squarer, to third slip and gully. Every captain has to pick where the gaps are.\n\nFourth slip or a fielder in the gap: what's your call? Comment 👇\n\n#CricketTactics #SlipCordon #FastBowling #TestCricket #Cricket"
  },
  {
    "id": "reel-ex14-round-the-wicket",
    "type": "reel",
    "when": "2026-11-22T19:30:00+05:30",
    "media": [
      "media/reel-ex14-round-the-wicket/1-reel.mp4"
    ],
    "cover": "media/reel-ex14-round-the-wicket/2-cover.jpg",
    "caption": "Same bowler. Same spot. Different angle. Out. 🏏\n\nFrom over the wicket, a right-arm bowler's angle takes the ball away from a left-hander. Go round the wicket and the same delivery angles back in at the stumps, so LBW and bowled come into play.\n\nBest bowler against left-handers you've seen? Comment 👇\n\n#CricketTactics #RoundTheWicket #LBW #TestCricket #Cricket"
  },
